IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je21-nouns`
IMPORT `je21-art03-commencement`

-- je21-tests-art03-commencement: tests for Article 3 (Commencement of Jersey legislation).
-- Every expected value below was written by hand from the text of Article 3 and the endnote (Part 2 in force on 28 September 2021) before the module was run.
-- Calendar facts used: 2024 is a leap year, 2023 is not, and a day after 31 January, 28 February (2023), 28 February (2024) and 31 December is as the calendar says.
-- Each rule has one case per branch, both sides of every day edge, and both readings of the forks L1, L2 and L3.

§ `Article 3 -- tests`

§§ `Names for the readings (the first of each pair is the default)`

`L1 default` MEANS `the Law does not say at what time of that day, so a question about a time of day on it is refused`
`L1 beginning` MEANS `the provision is in force from the beginning of that day`
`L2 default` MEANS `a stated time of day is provision to the contrary, and the legislation comes into force at that time`
`L2 beginning` MEANS `a stated time of day does not displace the beginning of the day`
`L3 default` MEANS `the beginning of 28 September 2021, by Article 3(2)`
`L3 refuse` MEANS `the sources do not state it, so a question that turns on a time of day on 28 September 2021 is refused`
`L12 exhaustive` MEANS `an applicability clause is exhaustive, so what lies outside it is not within the Article`
`L12 names only` MEANS `an applicability clause only names what it includes, so the Law does not say whether the Article reaches what lies outside it`

GIVEN h IS A NUMBER
      m IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Time of day`
`a time of day` h m MEANS `Time of day` OF h, m

§§ `3(1) A silent provision`

-- (a) legislation that only commences other legislation: in force when it is made, on the day it was made, from the time of making if known.
#ASSERT `Article 3(1): the moment a provision that is silent as to its commencement comes into force` `legislation having effect only to commence other legislation` (YMD 2022 3 10) (JUST (`a time of day` 10 15)) `L1 default` EQUALS `from the time it was made on the day` (YMD 2022 3 10) (JUST (`a time of day` 10 15))
#ASSERT `Article 3(1): the moment a provision that is silent as to its commencement comes into force` `legislation having effect only to commence other legislation` (YMD 2022 3 10) (JUST (`a time of day` 10 15)) `L1 beginning` EQUALS `from the time it was made on the day` (YMD 2022 3 10) (JUST (`a time of day` 10 15))
#ASSERT `Article 3(1): the moment a provision that is silent as to its commencement comes into force` `legislation having effect only to commence other legislation` (YMD 2022 3 10) NOTHING `L1 default` EQUALS `from the time it was made on the day` (YMD 2022 3 10) NOTHING
-- (a) an Act of the States referred to in Article 2(2): the same.
#ASSERT `Article 3(1): the moment a provision that is silent as to its commencement comes into force` `an Act of the States referred to in Article 2(2)` (YMD 2022 3 10) NOTHING `L1 default` EQUALS `from the time it was made on the day` (YMD 2022 3 10) NOTHING
#ASSERT `Article 3(1): the moment a provision that is silent as to its commencement comes into force` `an Act of the States referred to in Article 2(2)` (YMD 2022 3 10) (JUST (`a time of day` 23 59)) `L1 beginning` EQUALS `from the time it was made on the day` (YMD 2022 3 10) (JUST (`a time of day` 23 59))
-- (b) any other legislation: on the day after it is made, and the Law does not say at what time of that day (L1).
#ASSERT `Article 3(1): the moment a provision that is silent as to its commencement comes into force` `any other legislation` (YMD 2022 3 10) NOTHING `L1 default` EQUALS `at a time on the day that the Law does not state` (YMD 2022 3 11)
#ASSERT `Article 3(1): the moment a provision that is silent as to its commencement comes into force` `any other legislation` (YMD 2022 3 10) NOTHING `L1 beginning` EQUALS `from the beginning of the day` (YMD 2022 3 11)
-- A time of making is not used for (b): the day after is the day after, whatever the time on the day made.
#ASSERT `Article 3(1): the moment a provision that is silent as to its commencement comes into force` `any other legislation` (YMD 2022 3 10) (JUST (`a time of day` 23 59)) `L1 default` EQUALS `at a time on the day that the Law does not state` (YMD 2022 3 11)
-- The day after, across month ends, a leap day and a year end.
#ASSERT `Article 3(1): the moment a provision that is silent as to its commencement comes into force` `any other legislation` (YMD 2022 1 31) NOTHING `L1 beginning` EQUALS `from the beginning of the day` (YMD 2022 2 1)
#ASSERT `Article 3(1): the moment a provision that is silent as to its commencement comes into force` `any other legislation` (YMD 2023 2 28) NOTHING `L1 beginning` EQUALS `from the beginning of the day` (YMD 2023 3 1)
#ASSERT `Article 3(1): the moment a provision that is silent as to its commencement comes into force` `any other legislation` (YMD 2024 2 28) NOTHING `L1 beginning` EQUALS `from the beginning of the day` (YMD 2024 2 29)
#ASSERT `Article 3(1): the moment a provision that is silent as to its commencement comes into force` `any other legislation` (YMD 2023 12 31) NOTHING `L1 beginning` EQUALS `from the beginning of the day` (YMD 2024 1 1)

§§ `3(2) Legislation expressed to come into force on a particular day`

-- No time stated: the beginning of that day.
#ASSERT `Article 3(2): the moment legislation expressed to come into force on a particular day does so` (YMD 2018 6 1) NOTHING `L2 default` EQUALS `from the beginning of the day` (YMD 2018 6 1)
#ASSERT `Article 3(2): the moment legislation expressed to come into force on a particular day does so` (YMD 2018 6 1) NOTHING `L2 beginning` EQUALS `from the beginning of the day` (YMD 2018 6 1)
-- A time stated: provision to the contrary on the default reading (L2), the beginning of the day on the other.
#ASSERT `Article 3(2): the moment legislation expressed to come into force on a particular day does so` (YMD 2018 6 1) (JUST (`a time of day` 9 30)) `L2 default` EQUALS `from a stated time on the day` (YMD 2018 6 1) (`a time of day` 9 30)
#ASSERT `Article 3(2): the moment legislation expressed to come into force on a particular day does so` (YMD 2018 6 1) (JUST (`a time of day` 9 30)) `L2 beginning` EQUALS `from the beginning of the day` (YMD 2018 6 1)

§§ `Reading a moment: some time on a day`

-- "Was this regulation already in force on 1 June 2018?" -- the regulation is expressed to come into force on 1 June 2018.
`regulation of 1 June 2018` MEANS `Article 3(2): the moment legislation expressed to come into force on a particular day does so` (YMD 2018 6 1) NOTHING `L2 default`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 3: the provision was in force at some time on the day` `regulation of 1 June 2018` (YMD 2018 5 31)
#ASSERT `Article 3: the provision was in force at some time on the day` `regulation of 1 June 2018` (YMD 2018 6 1)
#ASSERT `Article 3: the provision was in force at some time on the day` `regulation of 1 June 2018` (YMD 2018 6 2)
-- Every constructor answers the day question the same way, with no refusal.
`silent regulation made on 10 March 2022` MEANS `Article 3(1): the moment a provision that is silent as to its commencement comes into force` `any other legislation` (YMD 2022 3 10) NOTHING `L1 default`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 3: the provision was in force at some time on the day` `silent regulation made on 10 March 2022` (YMD 2022 3 10)
#ASSERT `Article 3: the provision was in force at some time on the day` `silent regulation made on 10 March 2022` (YMD 2022 3 11)
#ASSERT `Article 3: the provision was in force at some time on the day` `silent regulation made on 10 March 2022` (YMD 2022 3 12)
`commencement Order made on 10 March 2022` MEANS `Article 3(1): the moment a provision that is silent as to its commencement comes into force` `legislation having effect only to commence other legislation` (YMD 2022 3 10) NOTHING `L1 default`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 3: the provision was in force at some time on the day` `commencement Order made on 10 March 2022` (YMD 2022 3 9)
#ASSERT `Article 3: the provision was in force at some time on the day` `commencement Order made on 10 March 2022` (YMD 2022 3 10)
`regulation in force from 9.30 a.m. on 1 June 2018` MEANS `Article 3(2): the moment legislation expressed to come into force on a particular day does so` (YMD 2018 6 1) (JUST (`a time of day` 9 30)) `L2 default`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 3: the provision was in force at some time on the day` `regulation in force from 9.30 a.m. on 1 June 2018` (YMD 2018 5 31)
#ASSERT `Article 3: the provision was in force at some time on the day` `regulation in force from 9.30 a.m. on 1 June 2018` (YMD 2018 6 1)

§§ `Reading a moment: a time of day on a day`

-- From the beginning of the day.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 3: the provision was in force at a time of day on the day` `regulation of 1 June 2018` (YMD 2018 5 31) (`a time of day` 23 59)
#ASSERT `Article 3: the provision was in force at a time of day on the day` `regulation of 1 June 2018` (YMD 2018 6 1) (`a time of day` 0 0)
#ASSERT `Article 3: the provision was in force at a time of day on the day` `regulation of 1 June 2018` (YMD 2018 6 1) (`a time of day` 23 59)
#ASSERT `Article 3: the provision was in force at a time of day on the day` `regulation of 1 June 2018` (YMD 2018 6 2) (`a time of day` 0 0)
-- From a stated time, 9.30 a.m.: both sides of the minute.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 3: the provision was in force at a time of day on the day` `regulation in force from 9.30 a.m. on 1 June 2018` (YMD 2018 5 31) (`a time of day` 23 59)
#ASSERT NOT `Article 3: the provision was in force at a time of day on the day` `regulation in force from 9.30 a.m. on 1 June 2018` (YMD 2018 6 1) (`a time of day` 0 0)
#ASSERT NOT `Article 3: the provision was in force at a time of day on the day` `regulation in force from 9.30 a.m. on 1 June 2018` (YMD 2018 6 1) (`a time of day` 9 29)
#ASSERT `Article 3: the provision was in force at a time of day on the day` `regulation in force from 9.30 a.m. on 1 June 2018` (YMD 2018 6 1) (`a time of day` 9 30)
#ASSERT `Article 3: the provision was in force at a time of day on the day` `regulation in force from 9.30 a.m. on 1 June 2018` (YMD 2018 6 1) (`a time of day` 9 31)
#ASSERT `Article 3: the provision was in force at a time of day on the day` `regulation in force from 9.30 a.m. on 1 June 2018` (YMD 2018 6 1) (`a time of day` 10 0)
#ASSERT `Article 3: the provision was in force at a time of day on the day` `regulation in force from 9.30 a.m. on 1 June 2018` (YMD 2018 6 1) (`a time of day` 23 59)
#ASSERT `Article 3: the provision was in force at a time of day on the day` `regulation in force from 9.30 a.m. on 1 June 2018` (YMD 2018 6 2) (`a time of day` 0 0)
-- From the time it was made, 2.00 p.m.
`commencement Order made at 2 p.m. on 10 March 2022` MEANS `Article 3(1): the moment a provision that is silent as to its commencement comes into force` `legislation having effect only to commence other legislation` (YMD 2022 3 10) (JUST (`a time of day` 14 0)) `L1 default`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 3: the provision was in force at a time of day on the day` `commencement Order made at 2 p.m. on 10 March 2022` (YMD 2022 3 9) (`a time of day` 23 59)
#ASSERT NOT `Article 3: the provision was in force at a time of day on the day` `commencement Order made at 2 p.m. on 10 March 2022` (YMD 2022 3 10) (`a time of day` 13 59)
#ASSERT `Article 3: the provision was in force at a time of day on the day` `commencement Order made at 2 p.m. on 10 March 2022` (YMD 2022 3 10) (`a time of day` 14 0)
#ASSERT `Article 3: the provision was in force at a time of day on the day` `commencement Order made at 2 p.m. on 10 March 2022` (YMD 2022 3 11) (`a time of day` 0 0)
-- From the time it was made, when the time is not known: a refusal on the day made, an answer on the days around it.
`commencement Order made at a time not known on 10 March 2022` MEANS `Article 3(1): the moment a provision that is silent as to its commencement comes into force` `legislation having effect only to commence other legislation` (YMD 2022 3 10) NOTHING `L1 default`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 3: the provision was in force at a time of day on the day` `commencement Order made at a time not known on 10 March 2022` (YMD 2022 3 9) (`a time of day` 12 0)
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 3: the provision was in force at a time of day on the day` `commencement Order made at a time not known on 10 March 2022` (YMD 2022 3 10) (`a time of day` 12 0) BECAUSE "the time of day at which the legislation was made is not given, so whether it was in force at a time of day on the day it was made cannot be answered"
#ASSERT `Article 3: the provision was in force at a time of day on the day` `commencement Order made at a time not known on 10 March 2022` (YMD 2022 3 11) (`a time of day` 0 0)
-- The day after it is made, default reading L1: the Law does not say at what time of that day.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 3: the provision was in force at a time of day on the day` `silent regulation made on 10 March 2022` (YMD 2022 3 10) (`a time of day` 23 59)
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 3: the provision was in force at a time of day on the day` `silent regulation made on 10 March 2022` (YMD 2022 3 11) (`a time of day` 8 0) BECAUSE "the Law does not say at what time of the day after it is made a provision that is silent as to its commencement comes into force"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 3: the provision was in force at a time of day on the day` `silent regulation made on 10 March 2022` (YMD 2022 3 11) (`a time of day` 0 0) BECAUSE "the Law does not say at what time of the day after it is made a provision that is silent as to its commencement comes into force"
#ASSERT `Article 3: the provision was in force at a time of day on the day` `silent regulation made on 10 March 2022` (YMD 2022 3 12) (`a time of day` 0 0)
-- The day after it is made, the other reading of L1: from the beginning of that day.
`silent regulation made on 10 March 2022, beginning-of-day reading` MEANS `Article 3(1): the moment a provision that is silent as to its commencement comes into force` `any other legislation` (YMD 2022 3 10) NOTHING `L1 beginning`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 3: the provision was in force at a time of day on the day` `silent regulation made on 10 March 2022, beginning-of-day reading` (YMD 2022 3 10) (`a time of day` 23 59)
#ASSERT `Article 3: the provision was in force at a time of day on the day` `silent regulation made on 10 March 2022, beginning-of-day reading` (YMD 2022 3 11) (`a time of day` 0 0)
#ASSERT `Article 3: the provision was in force at a time of day on the day` `silent regulation made on 10 March 2022, beginning-of-day reading` (YMD 2022 3 11) (`a time of day` 8 0)
-- A stated time, on the reading that does not let it displace the beginning of the day (L2).
`regulation of 1 June 2018 with a stated time, beginning-of-day reading` MEANS `Article 3(2): the moment legislation expressed to come into force on a particular day does so` (YMD 2018 6 1) (JUST (`a time of day` 9 30)) `L2 beginning`
#ASSERT `Article 3: the provision was in force at a time of day on the day` `regulation of 1 June 2018 with a stated time, beginning-of-day reading` (YMD 2018 6 1) (`a time of day` 0 0)

§§ `3(3) Regulations that commence by an Order of a Minister`

#ASSERT `Article 3(3): Regulations may provide that they commence by an Order of a Minister` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 3(3): Regulations may provide that they commence by an Order of a Minister` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 3(3): Regulations may provide that they commence by an Order of a Minister` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 3(3): Regulations may provide that they commence by an Order of a Minister` FALSE TRUE

§§ `3(4) Different days, times or events`

#ASSERT `Article 3(4): the power may specify different days, times or events for different provisions` TRUE TRUE `L12 exhaustive`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 3(4): the power may specify different days, times or events for different provisions` TRUE FALSE `L12 exhaustive`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 3(4): the power may specify different days, times or events for different provisions` FALSE TRUE `L12 exhaustive`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 3(4): the power may specify different days, times or events for different provisions` FALSE FALSE `L12 exhaustive`

-- Fork L12: a power outside the opening condition of Article 3(4) is not covered by it on the first reading, and the Law does not say on the second.
#ASSERT `Article 3(4): the power may specify different days, times or events for different provisions` TRUE TRUE `L12 names only`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 3(4): the power may specify different days, times or events for different provisions` TRUE FALSE `L12 exhaustive`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 3(4): the power may specify different days, times or events for different provisions` TRUE FALSE `L12 names only` BECAUSE "Article 3(4) speaks of a Law, Regulations made under a Law or a provision of either that may be commenced by Act or Order on a specified day, and the Law does not say whether it reaches any other power"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 3(4): the power may specify different days, times or events for different provisions` FALSE TRUE `L12 names only` BECAUSE "Article 3(4) speaks of a Law, Regulations made under a Law or a provision of either that may be commenced by Act or Order on a specified day, and the Law does not say whether it reaches any other power"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 3(4): the power may specify different days, times or events for different provisions` FALSE FALSE `L12 names only` BECAUSE "Article 3(4) speaks of a Law, Regulations made under a Law or a provision of either that may be commenced by Act or Order on a specified day, and the Law does not say whether it reaches any other power"

§§ `3(5) Amendment of uncommenced legislation`

#ASSERT NOT `Article 3(5)(a): the amendment of uncommenced legislation commences the legislation amended` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 3(5)(a): the amendment of uncommenced legislation commences the legislation amended` FALSE BECAUSE "Article 3(5) deals only with an amendment of legislation or a provision that has not come into force"

`the moment 1 June 2018` MEANS `from the beginning of the day` (YMD 2018 6 1)
`the moment 9.30 a.m. on 5 July 2018` MEANS `from a stated time on the day` (YMD 2018 7 5) (`a time of day` 9 30)
-- No provision made otherwise: the amendment commences when the provision amended commences.
#ASSERT `Article 3(5)(b): the moment at which the amendment commences` (JUST `the moment 1 June 2018`) FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST `the moment 1 June 2018`
#ASSERT `Article 3(5)(b): the moment at which the amendment commences` NOTHING FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- Provision made otherwise: the moment that provision gives.
#ASSERT `Article 3(5)(b): the moment at which the amendment commences` (JUST `the moment 1 June 2018`) TRUE (JUST `the moment 9.30 a.m. on 5 July 2018`) EQUALS JUST `the moment 9.30 a.m. on 5 July 2018`
#ASSERT `Article 3(5)(b): the moment at which the amendment commences` NOTHING TRUE (JUST `the moment 9.30 a.m. on 5 July 2018`) EQUALS JUST `the moment 9.30 a.m. on 5 July 2018`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 3(5)(b): the moment at which the amendment commences` (JUST `the moment 1 June 2018`) TRUE NOTHING BECAUSE "provision is made otherwise, and the moment it gives is not supplied"

§§ `3(6) Legislation that had commenced before Part 2 did`

-- Not commenced: Article 3 governs.
#ASSERT `Article 3(6): Article 3 governs when the legislation commenced` NOTHING `L3 default`
#ASSERT `Article 3(6): Article 3 governs when the legislation commenced` NOTHING `L3 refuse`
-- Commenced well before: Article 3 does not affect it.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 3(6): Article 3 governs when the legislation commenced` (JUST (YMD 2019 1 1)) `L3 default`
-- The edge: 27 September 2021 is before Part 2 came into force, 28 September 2021 is the day it did.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 3(6): Article 3 governs when the legislation commenced` (JUST (YMD 2021 9 27)) `L3 default`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 3(6): Article 3 governs when the legislation commenced` (JUST (YMD 2021 9 27)) `L3 refuse`
#ASSERT `Article 3(6): Article 3 governs when the legislation commenced` (JUST (YMD 2021 9 28)) `L3 default`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 3(6): Article 3 governs when the legislation commenced` (JUST (YMD 2021 9 28)) `L3 refuse` BECAUSE "the sources do not say at what time of day on 28 September 2021 Part 2 of the Law came into force, so whether legislation that commenced that day commenced before it cannot be answered"
#ASSERT `Article 3(6): Article 3 governs when the legislation commenced` (JUST (YMD 2021 9 29)) `L3 default`
#ASSERT `Article 3(6): Article 3 governs when the legislation commenced` (JUST (YMD 2021 9 29)) `L3 refuse`
#ASSERT `Article 3(6): Article 3 governs when the legislation commenced` (JUST (YMD 2024 1 11)) `L3 default`
